<p>Every report has a period filter and <span class="btnname">Excel</span> and <span class="btnname">Print</span> buttons.</p>
<table class="table table-sm">
    <thead><tr><th>Report</th><th>Shows</th></tr></thead>
    <tr><td>Income vs Expense</td><td>Month by month: sales, purchases, receipts, other income, expenses, supplier payments, net.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Inventory Usage (B2B/B2C)</td><td>Items used for B2B and B2C customers in a period, with value.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Supplier Summary</td><td>Opening, purchases, returns, paid, balance payable, open POs; <span class="btnname">Statement</span> per supplier.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Project Status</td><td>Active projects, current stage, who is assigned, days in stage.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Project Profit</td><td>Per project: invoice value before GST − material dispatched (at the rate of the purchase bill each piece came from, oldest stock first) − expenses linked to the project − EB / meter charges when the company pays them = profit, margin % and profit per kW. The same profit line shows at the top of each project page.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Subsidy Status</td><td>Subsidy projects with application no., status, amount, received date.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Customers: Cash / Loan</td><td>Cash and loan customers; loan amount, disbursed, pending, balance due.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Profit &amp; Loss</td><td>See Accounts.</td></tr>
</table>
<p>The <strong>Dashboard</strong> also shows cash / bank-loan client counts, total invoice value, paid and outstanding. Click a card to open the matching invoice list.</p>
